 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Not at all. It' kinder than showing up with a white cake and being asked, Is something wrong with flour? Then say, Sorry, I can't make it. Then offer to help find a replacement if it's just cake. Weddings are usually fully booked. Nothing. Just checking if you've thought about finding a replacement if you can't go. Then maybe just tell them you' sadly unable to cook due to your allergies. They might appreciate the honesty. If you can eat the standard wedding menu, then go for it. If you can't, carry only small bites. You don't have to explain yourself. Just tell them you' unfortunately unable to help with the food, and offer to find a replacement if they need one.",
